{"name":"Frozen Margarita","hex":"#dbe2cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frozen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having undergone the process of freezing; in ice form.","Immobilized."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of freeze"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frozen"},{"term":"margarita","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cocktail made with tequila, an orange-flavoured liqueur, and lemon or lime juice, often served with salt encrusted on the rim of the glass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/margarita"}],"entries":[{"title":"Margarita","blocks":[{"text":"A margarita is a cocktail of tequila, triple sec, lime juice, and sometimes simple syrup. It is served shaken with ice, without ice, or blended with ice (frozen). Most bars serve margaritas in a stepped-diameter variant of a cocktail glass or champagne coupe called a margarita glass, often with salt or Tajín on the rim of the glass. The margarita is one of the US most popular cocktails and the most popular tequila-based cocktail."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/MargaritaReal.jpg/330px-MargaritaReal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margarita","wikidata":"Q657621"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Balinese-room.jpg/500px-Balinese-room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Balinese-room.jpg/500px-Balinese-room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Balinese Room in Galveston, Texas","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABalinese-room.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Memorial_Day_margaritas.jpg/500px-Memorial_Day_margaritas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm